# The object a base constructor allocates belongs to the class whose prototype object arrives. The prototype object of another class selects an object of that class, below the constructor's class or not.
# Any other object leaves the site's own object, which then has another prototype than its layout: it gets ChangePrototype at the allocation, however that new.target arrived, here through a super call.
# The first prototype object of a constructor function is such an object: the property can be stored to, so the run time ties no object to the layout of a function.
